Feature: slice-6 / production-dns-cutover
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-6
Verified: 2026-05-28

What was built
==============
A reviewed runbook covering the production DNS cutover for both
launch domains:

  - superwizor.ai (apex)       → Firebase Hosting site superwizor-www
  - app.superwizor.ai          → Firebase Hosting site superwizor-app

Located at: docs/DNS_CUTOVER_RUNBOOK.md

The runbook is the operator cookbook to execute when launching. It
covers, in order:

  0. Pre-flight (T-24h) — green CI, green Lighthouse, Firebase Auth
     authorized-domains, OAuth redirect URIs across Google /
     Apple / Microsoft, GCS bucket CORS.
  1. Promote main to the live Hosting channel (T-1h) — for both
     sites; commands included.
  2. Connect custom domains in Firebase Console (T-0h) — apex
     uses A records (CNAMEs illegal at zone root); subdomain uses
     CNAME → superwizor-app.web.app. Recommended TTL of 300 during
     the cutover for fast rollback.
  3. Wait for SSL provisioning — managed Let's Encrypt, 2 min to
     24h; curl commands to monitor.
  4. Smoke test table — 7 endpoints across both hosts, expected
     responses for each.
  5. Post-cutover — restore TTLs, verify the /login redirect
     target, announce in #ops, watch error rate for 24h.
  6. Rollback plan — DNS-layer rollback (remove A/CNAME) and
     content-layer rollback (firebase hosting:rollback per site).
  7. Tracked follow-ups — Flutter Web CI deploy job, Terraform DNS
     module for future codification, CSP/SRI headers.

Why a runbook and not Terraform
================================
Today the project doesn't have a DNS terraform module. Adding one
just for this single cutover would expand scope; the launch is a
once-ever operation that benefits more from an explicit
human-readable checklist than from declarative infra. Terraform-
izing DNS is flagged as a follow-up under §7 of the runbook —
worth doing once a second environment (staging.superwizor.ai)
exists, at which point the module would have two callers.

Verification
============
- Cross-checked against the project's existing config:
  - firebase.json defines superwizor-www + superwizor-app exactly
    as the runbook expects (deploy commands match site names).
  - .github/workflows/marketing-site.yml `deploy-production` job
    already targets `target: superwizor-www, channelId: live` so
    step 1 for the marketing site is automatic on every main push.
  - storage.rules + superwizor-backend/infra/storage CORS comment
    confirm both origins are pre-whitelisted, matching §0.6.
  - next.config.ts (Slice 3) already redirects /login →
    https://app.superwizor.ai/login, so no app-side change is
    needed at cutover.

- The runbook is self-contained — every command + every
  registrar / console field name is spelled out. An operator with
  Firebase + GCP project-owner permissions and registrar admin
  rights can execute it end-to-end without external research.

